## The Bug

In `validate()`, the calorie-consistency check uses `>=` instead of `>`:

```cpp
if (std::fabs(declared - derived) >= tolerance) {
```

The spec says an ingredient is inconsistent only when `|declared - derived| > 0.1 * derived` — **strictly greater than** the 10% tolerance. A declared value that lies exactly on the 10% boundary (e.g. derived 300, declared 330) is *consistent* and must be accepted, but the current code throws on it. That's why the test "declared calories within ten percent are accepted and used" fails.

The fix is to change `>=` to `>` so the comparison matches the specification exactly. The header file is unchanged; only the source file needs correcting.

