1. `seenIndices.has(indexToken)` → `seenIndices.has(index)` and `seenIndices.add(indexToken)` → `seenIndices.add(index)` — the set now tracks numeric values, so `1` and `01` correctly collide and throw `Line 3: duplicate stop index 1`.
2. `s.index > b.index` → `s.index < b.index` in the tie-break — among stops with equal `close` and `open`, the smallest index now wins, so your example returns `[{ index: 1, ... }, { index: 2, ... }]`.

