`ddddd` is `(sum of the UTF-16 code units of every character from the start of the record up
to and including the '\n' that precedes the CHK line) modulo 100000`, written in decimal,
zero-padded to 5 digits.

The decoder accepts a record with or without a final `\n` after the CHK line, but the record
must otherwise use `\n` as the only line separator.

