## Summary of changes

1. **`isLeapYear`** — now implements the full Gregorian rule (`year % 4 === 0 && (year % 100 !== 0 || year % 400 === 0)`). Since `daysInMonth` is shared, this fixes both `encodeBill` and `decodeBill`: `1900-02-29` is now rejected with `invalid entry time` everywhere, while `2024-02-29` and `2000-02-29` still pass.

2. **`decodeBill` entry ordering check** — changed `time <= prevTime` to `time < prevTime`, so entries with identical timestamps decode successfully (matching the encoder's behavior and the spec's "non-decreasing" requirement).

