The fix is in the remainder-distribution loop:

```rust
while remainder > 0 {
    let idx = cursor % allocations.len();
    allocations[idx].1 += 1;
    remainder -= 1;
    cursor += 1;
}
```

The original `allocations[cursor % allocations.len()].1 += 1` tried to mutably borrow `allocations` for the index expression while immutably borrowing it (via `.len()`) inside that same expression. Computing `idx` first separates the immutable borrow from the mutable one, so the borrow checker is satisfied. Everything else is unchanged.

