# Building Permit Workflow Engine

A municipal building department needs a small state machine that tracks building permit applications from registration to a final decision. Implement a library crate with module name `permit_workflow_engine` exposing the types and functions below. Only the standard library may be used.

## Public constants

- `pub const PERMIT_FEE: u32 = 150;` — the fixed application fee, in whole currency units, charged once per permit.
- `pub const MAX_REVISION_ROUNDS: u32 = 3;` — the maximum number of times a reviewer may send an application back for revisions.

## Public types

`PermitStatus`, the lifecycle state of one application:

    pub enum PermitStatus {
        Draft, Submitted, UnderReview, RevisionsRequested,
        Approved, Rejected, Withdrawn, Expired,
    }

It must derive `Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq`.

`PermitRecord`, an immutable snapshot of one application, deriving `Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq`:

    pub struct PermitRecord {
        pub id: u32,
        pub address: String,
        pub status: PermitStatus,
        pub fee_paid: u32,          // min(total collected, PERMIT_FEE)
        pub outstanding_fee: u32,   // PERMIT_FEE - fee_paid, so 0 when overpaid
        pub revision_rounds: u32,   // number of completed revision requests
        pub rejection_reason: Option<String>, // Some only after a successful reject
    }

`WorkflowError`, deriving `Debug, PartialEq, Eq`:

    pub enum WorkflowError {
        UnknownPermit(u32),
        NotDraft { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        NotSubmitted { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        NotUnderReview { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        NotRevisionsRequested { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        NotWithdrawable { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        NotActive { id: u32, current: PermitStatus },
        UnpaidFee { id: u32, outstanding: u32 },
        RevisionLimitReached { id: u32 },
    }

## The registry

All behaviour lives on `pub struct PermitRegistry`, created with `PermitRegistry::new()`. It stores permits keyed by numeric id; ids start at 1 for the first registered permit and increase by exactly 1 for each subsequent registration. The registry is the only owner of the data; tests use only the public methods.

### Methods

- `pub fn register(&mut self, address: String) -> u32`
  Creates a new permit in `Draft` with no fees collected, no revision rounds, and no rejection reason. The address is stored verbatim. Returns the new id. This method cannot fail.

- `pub fn pay_fee(&mut self, id: u32, amount: u32) -> Result<u32, WorkflowError>`
  Adds `amount` to the total collected for the permit and returns the outstanding balance `max(PERMIT_FEE - total_collected, 0)`. Payments are accepted in **any** status, including terminal ones (refunds are out of scope), and an amount of 0 is allowed. Overpaying is permitted: once the total reaches `PERMIT_FEE` the outstanding balance stays 0. Unknown id → `UnknownPermit(id)`.

- `pub fn submit(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only a `Draft` permit can be submitted. Check order: unknown id → `UnknownPermit(id)`; wrong status → `NotDraft { id, current }`; unpaid fee → `UnpaidFee { id, outstanding }` where `outstanding` is the current balance. On success the status becomes `Submitted`.

- `pub fn start_review(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only `Submitted` → `UnderReview`; otherwise `NotSubmitted { id, current }`.

- `pub fn request_revisions(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only `UnderReview`; otherwise `NotUnderReview { id, current }`. If the permit is under review but already has `MAX_REVISION_ROUNDS` revision rounds, return `RevisionLimitReached { id }` and leave the status unchanged. Otherwise increment `revision_rounds` and set the status to `RevisionsRequested`. Check order: status check first, then the limit.

- `pub fn resubmit(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only `RevisionsRequested` → `UnderReview` (no new fee, `revision_rounds` unchanged); otherwise `NotRevisionsRequested { id, current }`.

- `pub fn approve(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only `UnderReview` → `Approved`; otherwise `NotUnderReview { id, current }`. Approving is always allowed while under review, even at the revision limit.

- `pub fn reject(&mut self, id: u32, reason: String) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Only `UnderReview` → `Rejected`; otherwise `NotUnderReview { id, current }`. The reason is stored and appears as `Some(reason)` in the record.

- `pub fn withdraw(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Allowed from `Draft`, `Submitted`, `UnderReview`, or `RevisionsRequested` → `Withdrawn`; from any terminal status (`Approved`, `Rejected`, `Withdrawn`, `Expired`) → `NotWithdrawable { id, current }`.

- `pub fn expire(&mut self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Allowed from the same four non-terminal statuses → `Expired`; from any terminal status → `NotActive { id, current }`.

- `pub fn status(&self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitStatus, WorkflowError>`
  Returns the current status; `UnknownPermit(id)` for an unknown id.

- `pub fn record(&self, id: u32) -> Result<PermitRecord, WorkflowError>`
  Returns a snapshot as described under `PermitRecord`; `UnknownPermit(id)` for an unknown id.

## General rules

- A failed call must never change any state (fees, status, rounds, reason all stay as they were).
- All mutating and querying methods (everything except `register`) return `UnknownPermit(id)` when the id is not registered, checked before any other rule.
- Every method that performs a transition returns the resulting `PermitStatus` on success.

## Examples

Submitting before paying fails, and nothing changes:

    let mut registry = PermitRegistry::new();
    let id = registry.register("12 Elm Street".to_string());
    assert_eq!(registry.submit(id), Err(WorkflowError::UnpaidFee { id, outstanding: 150 }));
    assert_eq!(registry.status(id).unwrap(), PermitStatus::Draft);

A happy path:

    let mut registry = PermitRegistry::new();
    let id = registry.register("12 Elm Street".to_string());
    registry.pay_fee(id, 150).unwrap();
    assert_eq!(registry.submit(id).unwrap(), PermitStatus::Submitted);
    assert_eq!(registry.start_review(id).unwrap(), PermitStatus::UnderReview);
    assert_eq!(registry.approve(id).unwrap(), PermitStatus::Approved);

