## The cause

The bug is in the `--level=N` handling in `parse()`. The duplicate check is nested **inside** the `Ok(n) if (1..=9).contains(&n)` match arm, so it only runs after the value has been successfully parsed and validated:

```rust
if let Some(value) = arg.strip_prefix("--level=") {
    match value.parse::<u32>() {
        Ok(n) if (1..=9).contains(&n) => {
            if level_seen {
                return Err(BackupError::DuplicateOption("--level".to_string()));
            }
            ...
        }
        _ => {
            return Err(BackupError::InvalidLevel(value.to_string()));
        }
    }
    ...
}
```

So with `--level=3 --level=nope`, the second occurrence fails `value.parse::<u32>()` and falls into the `_` arm, returning `InvalidLevel("nope")` before the duplicate check is ever reached. The spec requires that "the duplicate check happens **before** the second value is validated."

The fix is to check `level_seen` immediately after stripping the `--level=` prefix, before attempting to parse the value.

